    {
      "title": "Time + place + verb",
      "explain": "The usual Cantonese order is who → when → where → what: 我哋 (ngo5 dei6) + 七點 (cat1 dim2) + 喺門口 (hai2 mun4 hau2) + 等 (dang2). The time word can also go first: 七點我哋喺門口等 (cat1 dim2 ngo5 dei6 hai2 mun4 hau2 dang2). But the place (喺 (hai2)…) always comes before the verb.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "We'll meet at seven at the entrance.",
          "parts": [
